# Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (Unreal Engine 5, DirectX 12)
# Tested 2026-10-15 on a MacBook Air M4 with 16 GB, macOS 27.2, Steam build 1788652215.
# D3DMetal: plays at a steady ~35 fps at 1280x832 on the lowest preset, smoother than DXMT. At the
# panel's native 2560x1664 the title screen runs at ~37 fps and gameplay at 8-10 fps (GPU-bound).
# DXMT with -dx11: 25-35 fps but shadows render as a large checkerboard (DXMT bug), so not used.
# FSR, r.Streaming.PoolSize and D3DM_SUPPORT_DXR=0 made no measurable difference.
#! rating=playable
#! tested=MacBook Air (M4, 16 GB)
#! note=About 35 fps at 1280×832 on the lowest preset. It plays, but looks rough.
#! note=Set the resolution in the game (Settings → Graphics) to about half your screen's: at full resolution it runs at under 10 fps.
#! note=Keep the Backend on D3DMetal: DXMT draws the shadows as a checkerboard.
CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=d3dmetal
